{"nodes": [{"id": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___director_brief_25ddbbe5", "label": "Self-roster Fairness - Director Brief", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Director Brief_25ddbbe5.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___director_brief_25ddbbe5_two_round_vote", "label": "Two-Round Vote and One-Cycle Trial", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Director Brief_25ddbbe5.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Change process designed for legitimacy: anonymous two-round Microsoft Forms vote, one response per person - round 1 picks the top two options, round 2 is a head-to-head. The winner runs ONE roster cycle as an explicit trial, reviewed against staff sentiment plus an equity summary of how weekends, evenings and on-call actually fell; revert if it does not earn its place - nothing is permanent. Guarantee stated up front: no option changes quotas, coverage minimums or safe-hours rules, and none carries a cost."}, {"id": "graphify_out_converted_self_roster_fairness___director_brief_25ddbbe5_option_c_recommendation", "label": "Director Recommendation of Option C", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "graphify-out/converted/Self-roster Fairness - Director Brief_25ddbbe5.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Option C recommended because it removes the race and the feeling of one, everyone still chooses their own days, it is explainable in one breath, and it self-corrects - whoever misses a contested day holds priority for the next. Option D is the close second: same engine as C plus weighting for the days that matter most, right only if the group wants that control 